.SH NAME
SystemEx.Device.Memory.DeviceSharedBuffer< TDeviceSharedBackend > \- Represents a shared memory bridge between a \fBDeviceBuffer\fP and a hardware‑specific backend implementing \fBIDeviceSharedBackend\fP\&. 
.br
 Manages the lifecycle of a hardware buffer, including creation, upload, download, and cleanup, depending on the configured \fBSharedCacheType\fP\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SS "Public Member Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "bool \fBBegin\fP ()"
.br
.RI "Begins a shared memory session by locking the cache and creating the appropriate hardware buffer\&. 
.br
 For \fBSharedCacheType\&.ReadOnly\fP, a read buffer is created\&. 
.br
 For \fBSharedCacheType\&.WriteOnly\fP and \fBSharedCacheType\&.ReadWrite\fP, the cache contents are uploaded to a write buffer\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "void \fBEnd\fP ()"
.br
.RI "Ends the shared memory session by downloading data from the hardware buffer when required and unlocking the cache\&. 
.br
 For write‑enabled modes, the backend writes modified data back into the cache\&. 
.br
 For read‑only mode, the hardware buffer is simply closed\&. "
.in -1c
